course: dictionary
lesson: 1747
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word class is a good example. «Theo tells the whole class a joke, start to finish, and it's a good one.» Here class means the group of students who learn together, because a whole group can hear a joke.
explain: «Josh started falling asleep in class and his marks dropped a whole grade.» Here class means a lesson, a time of teaching. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try that meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Context can also show a casual meaning. «That goal was class!» has nothing to do with school. Class means excellent, because a great goal is praised, not sorted into a group.
fact: Class has many meanings, so check the sentence before you decide what it means.
fact: A class is a group of students who learn together.
fact: A class can be a lesson or a time of teaching: «a dance class».
fact: A class can be a group of things that are alike: «Mammals are a class of animals».
fact: In casual talk, «class» (UK, Ireland) means excellent: «That goal was class!»
exercise: «Theo tells the whole class a joke.» In this sentence, what does class mean? | A kind of animal | A seat on a train | *A group of students who learn together | A lesson about jokes
exercise: «Mammals are a class of animals.» What does class mean here? | Excellent | A ticket with extra room | *A group of things that are alike | A lesson in a school hall
exercise: «That goal was class!» In this sentence, what does class mean? | A mark out of ten | *Excellent | Sitting in a row | A kind of animal
test: «Josh started falling asleep in class.» What does class mean here? | A group of animals | Excellent | *A lesson or time of teaching | A group of people with the same money
test: In exams, which formal word can mean a group of students? | Casual | Classy | *Cohort | Classify
exam: «Ruby's teacher showed the class three questions that settle almost any claim.» What does class mean here? | *The students in a lesson | A ticket type | To sort into groups | Excellent
